{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-342023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=8x$ defined on $[-2,2).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $4$-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)=4{x}^{2}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n8x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070232/state.json" "file_sha256" "be6dc21a294a0d1b73c224ae73ac3fae765ba877b364b5d6a82506f3469b6309"} {"question" "q-342023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an odd function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and we are already given the coefficients ${b}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-2,2).$ \nTherefore, the $4$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}8t\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ [4{t}^{2}]_{0}^{x} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\cdot [-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{2})]_{0}^{x} \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{64(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070232/state.json" "file_sha256" "be6dc21a294a0d1b73c224ae73ac3fae765ba877b364b5d6a82506f3469b6309"} {"question" "q-342023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070232/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6e871d80cfa235b9b0b5332a2a10330f89050a626ed75eae4f97e1ff6c6d377f"} {"question" "q-342023" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070232/state.json" "file_sha256" "be6dc21a294a0d1b73c224ae73ac3fae765ba877b364b5d6a82506f3469b6309"} {"question" "q-342023" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2n\\pi x)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2n\\pi x)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070232/state.json" "file_sha256" "be6dc21a294a0d1b73c224ae73ac3fae765ba877b364b5d6a82506f3469b6309"} {"question" "q-342023" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070232/state.json" "file_sha256" "be